A||||14||MooCow||What to look for on a n 84?||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||12-04-2000||10:47 PM||||I am looking at buying an 84 stick Fiero for my winter beast.  The car looks to be in great shape and has 124,000 miles on it.  It has some good rims and tires.  Has a spoiler and the wholecar is painted a metalic red color.  I have not taken it for a test drive yet.  The thing is what should I ask for it?  The person right now has a $1,500 obo. I am selling my 86 SE for cheaper than that and mine is a v6.  What should I check for?  I am going to offer them about $800 cash on the spot if it runs good.  How do I tell if the clutch is going out?  Also what problems should I look for on this 84?<P>                               Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||12-04-2000||10:52 PM||||Arn't the only 84 fieros with spoilers indys?||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||12-04-2000||11:13 PM||||Trust me this is no indy.  It looks to be a stock spoiler that they must have put on.  This doesn't look like an Indy at all.  The nose is far from an Indy nose.  If it was then they changed the looks of it.<P>                               Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||12-05-2000||12:29 AM||||Hmmm... must have been something the guy added, post dealer option maybe?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Check to see if the volts are good, headlights work, etc.  Battery old?  Ask when the clutch was last replaced.  Ask when the last time it caught fire?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> j/k<P>If you buy it, you may want to check or replace the alternator belt just in case, mine broke.<P><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||jch82||12-05-2000||10:09 AM||||im going with to test drive the car! i cant wait. see ya then.<P>Josh||||reg||6
Z||000005||ROB MAC||12-05-2000||11:58 AM||||Look in the trunk - upper sides , pull back the carpet - look for big rusty holes||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||12-05-2000||05:34 PM||||Here's how to check a clutch:<P>Start the engine.<BR>Sink the clutch and put the shifter in 1st. Pull the shifter into neutral while keeping the clutch pedal down.<BR>Keep the clutch down while twiddling your thumbs for 10 seconds.<BR>Move the shifter into reverse without putting into any other gears first.<BR>If it grinds going into reverse then the clutch isn't releasing completely.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||12-05-2000||09:21 PM||||Heres what to look for....another car! $1500 is a (eh hem) bit much for an 84 w/ 124K on the clock...especially being a 4 banger...||||reg||1
Z||000008||William Federle||12-05-2000||10:05 PM||||I'd check underneath - all the places you grease. For that kind of money all of the ball joints and tie-rod ends should have good seals and show signs of regular lube.<P>And it shouldn't leak oil or burn it visibly.<P>Otherwise, offer 500.00. That's what I paid for mine and those are the major things wrong with it.<P>It doesn't have a spoiler - I guess that would add whatever it costs to put one on.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||MooCow||12-06-2000||08:52 AM||||Well jch82 and I went and test drove the 84 last night in about 3 inches of snow. It started right up and the idle is set at 2RPM's.  The gas petal was hard as a rock to push in.  There was no just tapping the gas you had to slam the gas but then the car would rise to about 3-4 RPM's way to quick.  From the outside the car sounded great and ran great besides the gas pedal sticking.  The clutch was brand new and felt very tight.  I asked the guy what he wanted for it and he said he was asking $1,500 but would take less.  I want to know how and what needs to be done to fix the gas pedal?  The headliner was very very low. The side of the seat was tore pretty badley.  Both headlight went up but on slower than the other.  the tires and rims are great alongg with the brakes.  The lock for the trunk isn't there and needs to be put back on.  I really didn't look for rust since this car is going to be a winter beater anyways.  I liked driving the car and sounded great but I couldn't get past 30 MPH and the gas pedal made it impossible to go with out spinning the tires.  What should I offer him?  He said the paint job was $1,200 and the tires were $800 but this guy is kinda out there.<P>                            Thanks Ken||||reg||4
Z||000010||PlasticWrapd||12-06-2000||09:25 AM||||Tell him that it'll take some real bucks to replace the throttle cable and get all the bugs worked out.  If that car runs VERY well and the clutch seems okay, then offer him $700.  The throttle cable can probably be lubed with graphite along with all the linkages.  Check to see if someone put a large return spring on the throttle body.  That's what someone did to mine to try and counteract a sticking cable.  I lubed the cable and removed the spring and all was fine.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tigger||12-06-2000||09:43 AM||||I'd agree, headliner can be fixed for about $30-45.  The throttle spring could be the cause if it's not stock.  Easy to see/check that one.<P>BTW, can you still buy throttle return springs for the 4 cyl?   Last time I was at a parts store they did't have one. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||DavidHenshaw||12-06-2000||06:39 PM||||A 4cyl with over 100k miles and the problems you are aware of should not cost more than $800 to $1,000 tops. And then there are the problems you don't know about yet but will learn about after you buy it. IMHO offer $500 and if you can't get the seller back to earth keep looking.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000013||beachbomb||12-06-2000||07:43 PM||||HI, just my two cents, i didn't pay $1,500 for either one of my two Indy's, i'd pass on it if he won't come down any, just my thoughts, jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||6
Z||000014||MooCow||12-07-2000||12:00 AM||||As soon as the weather clear up and no more snow is on the ground I am going to test drive it again.  Last time I never got past 3rd gear.  Actually never went faster than 25 MPH.  The worst thing about the car is the gas pedal sticking badley and the headliner hitting your head as you drive.  I will let you know how it turns out.<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||1
